    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Translate sentence-level JSON produced by media asr without rerunning ASR.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input JSON file produced by media asr.\r\n          --source-language TEXT \r\n                              Optional source language; defaults to the ASR JSON value or Auto.\r\n          --target-language TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Translation target language, e.g. zh-CN, en-US, ja-JP.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the translated sentence JSON to this path.\r\n          --timeout <duration> [5min] \r\n                              Maximum translation duration. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s,\r\n                              or min. Bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media translate --input /tmp/asr.json --target-language zh-CN\r\n  $ lyra-cli media translate --input /tmp/asr.json --source-language ja-JP --target-language zh-CN --output /tmp/asr.zh.json\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - Input must contain a sentence array from media asr.\r\n  - Sentence timing and source text are preserved; translation is added per sentence.\r\n  - This command does not read media, run ASR, or modify a draft.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Translate sentence-level JSON produced by media asr without rerunning ASR.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input JSON file produced by media asr.\r\n          --source-language TEXT \r\n                              Optional source language; defaults to the ASR JSON value or Auto.\r\n          --target-language TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Translation target language, e.g. zh-CN, en-US, ja-JP.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the translated sentence JSON to this path.\r\n          --timeout <duration> [5min] \r\n                              Maximum translation duration. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s,\r\n                              or min. Bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media translate --input /tmp/asr.json --target-language zh-CN\r\n  $ lyra-cli media translate --input /tmp/asr.json --source-language ja-JP --target-language zh-CN --output /tmp/asr.zh.json\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - Input must contain a sentence array from media asr.\r\n  - Sentence timing and source text are preserved; translation is added per sentence.\r\n  - This command does not read media, run ASR, or modify a draft.\r\n",
